(7738563, 1275944, 27608, '<td valign="top">Thanks very much everyone!  Happy to see another ribbon and very unexpected.  I wasn''t super happy Stark was butted up against the edge of the frame.  But I liked the wind blowing Nova''s hair and Stark stalking her LOL.  Lucky dogs indeed on DPC.  They are the reason I got back into photography this year after my eldest dog peacefully passed away in June (14.5 yers old).  I love to take pictures of them.  My old 5DmkII just couldn''t keep up with them AF wise, but this R5 is incredible.  My wife was the one to suggest we get a new camera and glass as I created Teague''s celebration video.  The younger pups hardly had any good quality pics.  The timing was ideal for mirrorless.  Hopefully I can find a balance so I don''t saturate the site LOL.<br/> <br/>The Pack<br/><a href="https://www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=1276115" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img border="0" src="https://images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/25000-29999/27608/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_1276115.jpg" xalt="'' . substr(''https://images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/25000-29999/27608/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_1276115.jpg'', strrpos(''https://images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/25000-29999/27608/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_1276115.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''"/></a> <br/> <br/>Teague (2008-2022) - <a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=sjdg8pxtduU" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">Celebrating Teague (youtube)</a> <br/><a href="https://www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=936504" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img border="0" src="https://images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/25000-29999/27608/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_936504.jpg" xalt="'' . substr(''https://images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/25000-29999/27608/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_936504.jpg'', strrpos(''https://images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/25000-29999/27608/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_936504.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''"/></a> <br/> <br/>Cole - he is getting on in age and his back legs are getting weak.  His time is approaching I fear :''(<br/><a href="https://www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=995619" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img border="0" src="https://images.dpchallenge.com/images_challenge/1000-1999/1519/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_995619.jpg" xalt="'' . substr(''https://images.dpchallenge.com/images_challenge/1000-1999/1519/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_995619.jpg'', strrpos(''https://images.dpchallenge.com/images_challenge/1000-1999/1519/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_995619.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''"/></a> <a href="https://www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=952267" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img border="0" src="https://images.dpchallenge.com/images_challenge/1000-1999/1387/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_952267.jpg" xalt="'' . substr(''https://images.dpchallenge.com/images_challenge/1000-1999/1387/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_952267.jpg'', strrpos(''https://images.dpchallenge.com/images_challenge/1000-1999/1387/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_952267.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''"/></a> <br/> <br/>Nova &amp; Stark<br/><a href="https://www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=1275760" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img border="0" src="https://images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/25000-29999/27608/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_1275760.jpg" xalt="'' . substr(''https://images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/25000-29999/27608/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_1275760.jpg'', strrpos(''https://images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/25000-29999/27608/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_1275760.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''"/></a><br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2023-02-15 07:54:17.</i></td>', 'Thanks very much everyone!  Happy to see another ribbon and very unexpected.  I wasn''t super happy Stark was butted up against the edge of the frame.  But I liked the wind blowing Nova''s hair and Stark stalking her LOL.  Lucky dogs indeed on DPC.  They are the reason I got back into photography this year after my eldest dog peacefully passed away in June (14.5 yers old).  I love to take pictures of them.  My old 5DmkII just couldn''t keep up with them AF wise, but this R5 is incredible.  My wife was the one to suggest we get a new camera and glass as I created Teague''s celebration video.  The younger pups hardly had any good quality pics.  The timing was ideal for mirrorless.  Hopefully I can find a balance so I don''t saturate the site LOL. The Pack  Teague (2008-2022) - Celebrating Teague (youtube)   Cole - he is getting on in age and his back legs are getting weak.  His time is approaching I fear :''(   Nova & Stark', '2023-02-15 07:34:42.000000', '2023-02-15 07:54:17.000000', 0),
